{"availability":"available","full":"HastH8/LocaleForge","name":"LocaleForge","description":"AI-assisted localization for Lua, JSON, JavaScript, and TypeScript—without breaking code structure.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T18:17:40Z","updated":"2026-10-08T18:27:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://locale.hastherish.com","topics":["developer-tools","fivem","gemini","localization","nextjs","translation","typescript"],"demo":"https://locale.hastherish.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:29.773Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:29.773Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:29.773Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:29.773Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI-assisted localization for Lua, JSON, JavaScript, and TypeScript files—without accounts, dashboards, or damaged placeholders.","LocaleForge is a focused localization workspace for developers. Upload or paste a localization file, choose as many as 12 target languages, review each generated file in a syntax-aware editor, and download one file or a complete ZIP archive.","The server asks Gemini to translate only human-readable strings. It instructs the model to preserve keys, nesting, delimiters, comments, quote style, and common runtime placeholders, then checks the returned result before presenting it to the user."],"features":["No account required — open the translator and start immediately.","Developer-native formats — Lua, JSON, JavaScript, and TypeScript.","Broad language catalog — searchable target-language picker with native names and country flags.","Structure-aware prompts — keys, identifiers, paths, commands, and framework names stay untouched.","Placeholder validation — protects patterns including %{name}, {{count}}, ${value}, %s, %d, [E], r, and ^1."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HastH8/LocaleForge/blob/main/RE